    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27549" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maecĭus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mētĭus</span></b> ), i,
			m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the name of a place in Latium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nec procul ab Lanuvio (ad Maecium is locus
					dicitur) castra oppugnare est adortus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					6, 2, 8</span></i>
			 (dub.; Weissenb. ad Mecium).—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Maecĭa</span></b> ,
			ae, f., <i>a tribe</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				8, 17, 11</span></i>; <i><span class="en">29,
				37</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Planc. 16, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 4,
				15, 9</span></i>; Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				136</span></i> Müll.</div>
